{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1568793816,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0OTUwNTY3NTg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3683","origin":"github"},"title":"SSH Git server test setup difficult/non-functional","message":"After wasting a bit of time on the SSH issue in https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3638 I conclude that our test setup is not very useful for getting SSH **client** functionality confirmed working on windows. The reason is that even with OpenSSH server being install and working on appveyor or win10, a simple `git clone` will fail, because `git-upload-pack` is not found on the \"server\". The reason seems to be that git4win only makes commands accessible in the standard PATH via the main `git` entry point, but not individual commands that sit in `libexec/git-core`.","files":null}]}